From 44d63c2100d6b3eca63e536986955909e990fa24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahsan Hussain <ahsan.hussain@siemens.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:42:40 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] venus: stop spoofing VK_EXT_physical_device_drm on Nvidia
 for Wayland

Commit 1a302155ee2 ("venus: force prime blit on Nvidia GPU") hides
VK_EXT_physical_device_drm on Nvidia so that Wayland wsi always takes the
prime blit path. The reason is that compositors may offer only LINEAR,
which Nvidia can't render to, and that wsi could not reject LINEAR once
the native image path was taken. The previous commit makes common wsi
check the modifier tiling features and fall back to the buffer blit
itself in that case.

Report the real VK_EXT_physical_device_drm on Wayland again. Wayland wsi
then takes the zero-copy native path when the compositor offers a tiled
Nvidia modifier, e.g. a virgl compositor on a host with tiled Venus
interop allocation, and keeps the prime blit when it doesn't. The
same-GPU blit also allocates its LINEAR buffer from device memory
instead of system memory, as the device now matches the compositor's
DRM device.

The X11 part of the spoof (the PCI bus info, which X11 wsi uses to match
the device) and the gamescope exception are unchanged.

Tested with a Venus guest on an NVIDIA 595 host, Weston on virgl:
 - host with tiled interop: native path with tiled modifiers,
   vkmark --winsys=wayland 5396 (with the spoof: 1782)
 - host without it: LINEAR prime blit, 4207 (with the spoof: 2183)

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Ahsan Hussain <ahsan.hussain@siemens.com>
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c | 32 +++++++++++---------------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c
index e73ab48c2fe..60c565d320e 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_wsi.c
@@ -138,18 +138,18 @@ vn_wsi_init(struct vn_physical_device *physical_dev)
        physical_dev->renderer_driver_version <
           VN_MAKE_NVIDIA_VERSION(590, 48, 1, 0));
 
-   /* Normally Venus on Nvidia GPUs takes the prime blit path. The exception
-    * is when KWin or any wlroots based compositors are used:
-    * 1. KWin and wlroots based compositors always add LINEAR to dmabuf
-    *    feedback tranches assuming LINEAR can be handled by GPU drivers.
-    * 2. Venus + Virgl only sees the compositor injected LINEAR mod since
-    *    Virgl doesn't support explicit modifiers on the driver side.
-    * 3. Nvidia GPUs doesn't support LINEAR color attachment, and it's too
-    *    late to reject LINEAR mod when the native image path has already
-    *    been taken instead of the prime image path.
+   /* Venus on Nvidia GPUs takes the prime blit path on X11, since Nvidia
+    * GPUs don't support LINEAR color attachment.
     *
-    * Gamescope requires VK_EXT_physical_device_drm and its runtime doesn't
-    * use standard WSI extensions, so venus can spoof without impacting it.
+    * On Wayland, common wsi takes the native image path only if one of the
+    * compositor modifiers supports the swapchain usage, and falls back to
+    * the prime blit path otherwise. That covers compositors that only offer
+    * LINEAR (e.g. KWin and wlroots always add it, and Virgl without
+    * explicit modifier support has nothing else), while a compositor that
+    * offers a tiled Nvidia modifier gets zero-copy native images.
+    *
+    * Gamescope is excluded as before since its runtime doesn't use standard
+    * WSI extensions.
     */
    struct vk_properties *props = &physical_dev->base.vk.properties;
    const bool is_nvidia = props->vendorID == 0x10de;
@@ -162,16 +162,6 @@ vn_wsi_init(struct vn_physical_device *physical_dev)
       props->pciBus = 0;
       props->pciDevice = 0;
       props->pciFunction = 0;
-
-      /* Fail same_gpu check on wayland. See wsi_wl_display_init. */
-      physical_dev->base.vk.supported_extensions.EXT_physical_device_drm =
-         false;
-      props->drmHasPrimary = false;
-      props->drmHasRender = true;
-      props->drmPrimaryMajor = 0;
-      props->drmPrimaryMinor = 0;
-      props->drmRenderMajor = 0;
-      props->drmRenderMinor = 0;
    }
 
    const VkAllocationCallbacks *alloc =
-- 
